    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Vitamin and mineral deficiency diseases (e.g., Scurvy, Rickets, Anemia, Goitre) are frequently tested in objective questions.",
        "Key distinction: Kwashiorkor is primarily caused by protein deficiency, whereas Marasmus results from severe total caloric and protein deficiency.",
        "Caloric values of biomolecules: Carbohydrates and Proteins yield approximately 4 kcal/g, while Fats yield 9 kcal/g."
      ],
      "id": "zqhq7jn"
